$ONB $AVTR $FITB new factors

@Triplsex @Murdangamez we&#39;ve been focused on $IBM for a while, and IBM may still be a partner even if the impending announcement is another company. $MSFT invested in Fabrica over a decade ago - but that&#39;s also when Dagi was part of the team, and $GOOG belongs in the conversation as a dream partner. Or none of the above. 

One risk, even if it does turn out to be a dream partner, is that the contract value is not as exciting as hoped. These are interconnects, and the manufacturing platform to build them: we&#39;ve seen other contracts for about $500K for single AME production setups, so how many would a hyperscaler need? Maybe it&#39;s just $2M for a couple machines to start warming up, and maybe up to $10M total over 5 years. That&#39;s not gonna send this into launch mode. 

Dagi buying more with what he can scrape together (looks like his monthly salary for the last month), and the fact that insiders have not filed any sales, continue to be the primary sources of confidence in continuing to hold.

